### FastAPI Application - HTTP Test Queries

# Base URL - Update this to match your server
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### 1. Root Endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 2. Create a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "john.doe@example.com",
    "username": "johndoe",
    "full_name": "John Doe",
    "is_active": true
}

###

### 3. Create another user for testing
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "jane.smith@example.com",
    "username": "janesmith",
    "full_name": "Jane Smith",
    "is_active": true
}

###

### 4. Get all users (default pagination)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 5. Get all users with custom pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/?skip=0&limit=10
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 6. Get a specific user by ID (replace {user_id} with actual ID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 7. Get another user by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/2
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 8. Update a user (replace {user_id} with actual ID)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "john.updated@example.com",
    "username": "johnupdated",
    "full_name": "John Doe Updated",
    "is_active": true
}

###

### 9. Partial update of a user (only some fields)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "full_name": "Jane Smith Updated",
    "is_active": false
}

###

### 10. Delete a user (replace {user_id} with actual ID)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 11. Try to get a non-existent user (should return 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/999
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 12. Try to update a non-existent user (should return 404)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "nonexistent@example.com",
    "username": "nonexistent"
}

###

### 13. Try to delete a non-existent user (should return 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/999
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 14. Create a user with minimal data (only required fields)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "minimal@example.com",
    "username": "minimaluser"
}

###

### 15. Create a user with all optional fields
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "complete@example.com",
    "username": "completeuser",
    "full_name": "Complete User Profile",
    "is_active": false
}

###
